nce/mathacademy/question-capture/13931548/assets/288adf3d1da5cf4bb6e2530318aeb083b69d43639de7704f9df15672be477d0a.png)\n\nLet's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $f(x)={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x}$ is defined for all input values $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. For $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ falls. Therefore, $y=f(x)$ is a decreasing function.\n\n- Statement III is false. As $x$ increases, the function value gets smaller and smaller, approaching zero. Therefore $f(x)\\to 0$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and II are true." 13194139533642 true] [17592186243602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243603 13194139533642 true] [17592186243602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243604 13194139533642 true] [17592186243602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243605 13194139533642 true] [17592186243602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243606 13194139533642 true] [17592186243602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243607 13194139533642 true] [17592186243602 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533642 true] [17592186243602 1041 "selection" 13194139533642 true] [17592186243602 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243606 13194139533642 true] [17592186243602 1110 #uuid "4aa8b7b9-ea94-5244-87cf-e7f5bc4dbcb8" 13194139533642 true] [17592186243603 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533642 true] [17592186243603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533642 true] [17592186243603 1111 #uuid "9908dc27-d052-543b-948d-d8303f54e13d" 13194139533642 true] [17592186243604 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533642 true] [17592186243604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533642 true] [17592186243604 1111 #uuid "699806d4-fcdc-5a97-8c7a-45b83aa7a0b9" 13194139533642 true] [17592186243605 1034 "I only" 13194139533642 true] [17592186243605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533642 true] [17592186243605 1111 #uuid "f6a3e4bf-cbd7-51b1-b831-9e2289f8bcb5" 13194139533642 true] [17592186243606 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533642 true] [17592186243606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533642 true] [17592186